From: BananaOS Duo Lite maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Export the compatible VA 1.22 driver entry point

Electron 42 ships libva 2.22, while the firmware builds with libva 2.23.
The 2.22/2.23 va_backend.h context and vtable declarations are identical
(the only difference is an Android enum deprecation annotation). Export
both entry points and report the older API to the older loader.

--- a/src/driver.c
+++ b/src/driver.c
@@ -55,3 +55,15 @@
 {
     return venus_driver_init(context);
 }
+
+/* libva 2.22 (VA 1.22) and 2.23 have the same driver context/vtable ABI.
+ * Electron 42 bundles 2.22 and cannot discover a 1.23-only entry point. */
+#if VA_MAJOR_VERSION == 1 && VA_MINOR_VERSION > 22
+VENUS_PUBLIC VAStatus __vaDriverInit_1_22(VADriverContextP context)
+{
+    VAStatus status = venus_driver_init(context);
+    if (status == VA_STATUS_SUCCESS)
+        context->version_minor = 22;
+    return status;
+}
+#endif
